# Docker build context for docker/media-infra/Dockerfile.
#
# The CDK asset is defined with `directory: '.'`, so without this file the entire
# repository is both sent to the Docker daemon and folded into the asset
# fingerprint. That was 458 MB, including 281 MB of node_modules and 80 MB of
# fetched test video, which meant an unrelated edit (or a single ./fetch.sh run)
# changed the image hash and forced a container restart on the next deploy.
#
# Deny-list rather than allow-list: `*` excludes the top-level `docker`
# directory, and CDK stages the context before building, so the Dockerfile
# itself has to remain in it.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
**/node_modules
docker-container/dist
dist
cdk.out
.cdk.staging

# Test harness. test-streams/media holds large fetched video; including it made
# every fetch.sh run change the container image hash.
test-streams
test
coverage
*.lcov
jest.config.js

# CDK app and infrastructure sources. None of this is read by the Dockerfile,
# which only copies from docker-container/.
lib
bin
scripts
cdk.json
cdk.context.json
tsconfig.json
package.json
package-lock.json

# Docs and repository metadata
docs
*.md
LICENSE
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Compiled TypeScript emitted next to sources
**/*.js.map
**/*.d.ts

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cert

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
